---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import ContactForm from '../components/ContactForm.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site.config';
---
<Base title="Contact the AC to DC Editorial Team" description="Send a private calculator issue report, technical correction, or website question. Include your model, units, result and supporting reference."><div class="shell page-intro legal"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'Contact'}]}/><p class="eyebrow">CORRECTIONS & QUESTIONS</p><h1>Help make the explanation clearer.</h1><p>Report a calculation issue, suggest a technical correction, or ask about the website. Messages go to a private editorial inbox, not a public GitHub issue.</p><ContactForm/>{(site.contactEmail||site.issueUrl)&&<aside class="contact-box"><h2>Additional contact options</h2>{site.contactEmail&&<p>Public editorial email: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a></p>}{site.issueUrl&&<p><a href={site.issueUrl}>Open the public issue page</a>. Anything posted there is public; use the private form for personal details.</p>}</aside>}<div class="prose"><h2>What makes a useful report?</h2><p>Record the selected rectifier or regulator model, every active input with units, the result shown, and the value you expected. A datasheet, derivation or reputable source helps us assess a technical correction. This is an educational website; we cannot approve an installation or provide emergency electrical advice.</p><h2>What happens after sending?</h2><p>A successful submission displays a reference number. The owner can read it in the authenticated dashboard. There is no automatic email acknowledgment, promised response time or guaranteed engineering review. Messages have a 30-day inbox window; daily cleanup may take up to another 24 hours. Please keep a copy if you need your own record.</p></div></div></Base>
